    <DataNode elementId="AT3G16390-MONOMER" textLabel="AT3G16390-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT3G16390-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="450" centerY="395" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, zhang">Nitrile-specifier proteins (NSP) are independent of epithio-specifier proteins (ESP) in simple nitrile formation. There are five functional NSPs in the Arabidopsis genome. In vitro assay indicated that they act upon both aliphatic and aromatic glucosinolates. Indole glucosinolates were not tested in the study|CITS: [18987211]|.</Comment>
